WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.960
Section Chief Armor...

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.460
I can't do that!

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.380
He's right!

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.520
Let's end this!

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.320
I understand how you feel.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.240
But I need you to do this.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.630
Even Fullface and Okitsune-san 
complied in the end.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:18.980
Even they did?!

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.130
Impossible...

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:21.860
So...

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:25.250
Hurry up and just put the hats!

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:30.570
<b>Merry Christmas, Mr. Bookstore</b>

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.530
No way!

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:30.560
I got a job at a bookstore because 
I wanted to avoid that crap!

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.740
Is there <i>really</i> any reason
 the staff has to dress up?

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.740
There is, very much!

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:42.350
Ko***kame Complete Set

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:42.350
<b>San****shi</b>

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.710
We want to get our customers excited, 
and hopefully have them buy complete sets!

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:40.580
That crap's not selling!

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.340
They're gonna just buy it online!

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.470
If you don't wear them,

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:49.120
I'm gonna make you help with gift 
wrapping in the kid's books section!

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:55.460
*Think about what happens in the kid's 
books section at this time of year.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:50.830
Anything but that!

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.250
Anything but that, please!

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.840
I'd never survive that wrapping hell!

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:02.060
<i>Christmas: A demonic event 
that brings madness to all.</i>

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:08.940
<b>Why don't you have it?!
 You could have come earlier!</b>

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:08.940
<b>Customer</b>

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.900
<i>Customers descend into the 
pits of Hell when they've</i>

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.480
<i>waited too long to buy their gifts.</i>

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:13.270
<i>Store staff, frantically assembling complete 
sets of books that may not even sell.</i>

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:18.680
<i>What's supposed to be a holy night ends up 
somehow tearing at the soul instead.</i>

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.330
Ah, Honda!

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.160
I'm so glad you're here!

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.680
May I ask for your time?

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.860
Sure.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.570
My grandchild is coming over.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.880
What's a feel-good manga 
that's fit for Christmas?

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.490
<i>What do you mean by "feel-good"?</i>

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:42.040
Let me think...

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.140
If you want a feel-good adventure, this one.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:50.470
If you want a bittersweet romance that'll 
leave you feeling good, this one.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.460
Wow! I'll take this one, then.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.990
Thank you.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.280
Thanks, Honda.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:03.200
That granny was, like, "feel-good," so 
I almost took her to the BL shelves.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.290
<i>What a horrifying thought.</i>

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.860
Hey, hey, can I ask you something?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:10.960
Yes?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.870
Do you have that one book that won 
the, uh... what's-it award recently?

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.740
I want to buy it for my wife.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.910
Let's see...

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:18.870
What was it called again...

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:18.940
This one won an award recently.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.820
Oh, the one with a kanji name!

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.800
Or maybe this one?

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.270
That's totally not it, and I don't 
remember what it was, but whatever.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.300
Thanks!

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.300
<i>Seriously?! That's good enough?!</i>

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.860
<b>Helping people discover new books!</b>

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.440
This one, please.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.900
<b>San****shi</b>

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.050
<i>I-It sold!</i>

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.840
<b>Thank you...</b>

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.320
<i></i>San****shi <i>sold, Section Chief Armor!</i>

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.340
Oh, by the way...

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.160
Yes?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.800
Could you please gift wrap this?

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:59.460
W-W-We have wrapping paper
 as well as bags with ribbons.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.740
<i>Though, I can only handle the bags.</i>

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.220
Okay, then...

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:07.930
This one.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.150
Understood.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.980
It will take a moment. Is that acceptable?

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.180
Please feel free to browse
 the shop while you wait.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.950
<i>Th-Thank you so, so much.</i>

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:24.930
** Bookstore

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:24.460
All done, everyone!

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.610
Next up is the New Year's sale!

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.700
Although, the only difference 
is that we're switching

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.590
the Christmas pop-ups for the complete
 sets with New Year's mochi.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.440
We have something for you to wear, too.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.510
Here, mochi.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.830
Do you think we'll have customers 
for the New Year's holiday?

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:44.840
We have to pray we'll get people who 
want to come for the first sale.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.360
Are you sure that isn't too convenient?

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.990
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.120
<i>Once you hear this music,</i>

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:08.690
<b>It's Time to Close</b>

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:07.360
<i>it's time to close for the day.</i>

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.060
Good morning.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.110
Mornin'.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.680
Huh, did you have the late 
shift today, Honda-san?

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:17.520
Yes.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:21.160
<i>Broadly speaking, there are two 
shifts that the staff have.</i>

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.190
<i>The early shift, who work during the day,</i>

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:26.070
<b>Early shift</b>

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.070
<b>Late shift</b>

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.150
<i>and the late shift, who work at night.</i>

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:27.930
Good morning.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:30.100
Oh, good morning.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.420
Good morning.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:33.060
On the late shift today, huh?

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.560
I look forward to working with you.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:39.920
<i>These two—plus Houtai-san—
make the late shift dream team,</i>

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.180
<i>the pillars of the night shop, guiding 
all the part-timers at night.</i>

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:47.050
Where's the section chief today?

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.400
She's got the early shift.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.300
The manager's absent, huh?

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.600
I'm sorry.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.490
Section Chief Armor.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.350
I can't work overtime tonight.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:05:59.380
I'm sorry.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.530
Call the brass if anything ever comes up.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.740
That's seriously ominous.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.050
It's not that busy today.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.140
We'll be fine.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:09.980
You should go home on time for once.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:11.730
Huh? Really? You're so kind!

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:13.660
Thank you!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.970
Well, I mean, the boss has to do it, 
or the underlings will never learn.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:18.890
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.530
I swear, I'll do it right.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.700
Okay, here are the messages for the day.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.300
Okay!

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.390
<i>I like the looks on your faces.</i>

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:32.220
<i>These hand-picked elite part-timers,</i>

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.280
<i>trained by the late shift,</i>

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.570
<i>are a must-have for the business.</i>

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:40.950
Um...

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:42.970
The messages, please.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:47.330
** Bookstore

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.990
See you all!

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.280
Good work.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.030
Good work.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.990
Okay, then, sorry for 
leaving before all of you.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:56.990
Thanks for taking care of things.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:58.280
Pardon me.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.500
She's totally not ready to 
pass on to the next life.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:07.270
<b>The guy who talks to customers</b>

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.280
Your attention, please.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:21.800
Notice of closure to customers: Talking directly to customers can result in conflict, so they were taught to face the ceiling while talking. How considerate.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:13.580
The shop will soon be closing soon.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:22.020
If you would like to make a purchase, we kindly 
ask that you make your way to the registers.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.260
<b>The girls recording sales</b>

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.990
<b>Senpai rapidly counting money</b>

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.040
<i>Wow.</i>

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:32.350
<i>Everyone's totally in sync at night.</i>

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.830
<i>Man, I have to help with 
closing the registers next.</i>

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:39.240
<b>Honda standing at the door
 to keep customers out</b>

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:42.450
<i>I can never remember how to do it.</i>

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:48.410
<b>Spacing out...</b>

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:45.910
<i>I'm so bad at remembering how to do it 
that I'm constantly staring at my notes.</i>

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:48.150
<i>The late shift really is amazing.</i>

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:49.680
Honda-san!

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:56.890
<i>Crap, I let a customer in!</i>

00:07:56.890 --> 00:08:00.890
Sir, I'm sorry, we're closing for the night.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:05.340
<i>They're like Hollywood stars!</i>

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.020
<i>But never mind that...</i>

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.610
<i>Come to me, English power!</i>

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.670
Sorry, it's time to close for tonight!

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.090
Please come again!

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.410
Thank you very much.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.190
Good night!

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.450
Have a good night!

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.540
<i>Not bad, even if I did "good night" them twice.</i>

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.310
<i>Please be able to make out what I said!</i>

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.640
I'm sorry, I got it.

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.160
I'm very sorry about that!

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:30.930
And the exit is that way!

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:31.640
Sure.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:34.800
Thank you very much.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.370
The exit is this way.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:40.950
Customers clear!

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.210
Good work, everyone.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:48.330
<i>Even after the shop's closed, it's still busy
 with cleaning and re-stocking and such.</i>

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:48.340
Prepping new books

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:48.340
Cleaning

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:52.450
<i>Closing the registers is 
particularly prone to issues.</i>

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.710
<b>Cash overage/shortage</b>

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.710
<b>Actual</b>

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:55.980
<i>Yes!</i>

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.990
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:59.830
No discrepancy here.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.250
None here, either.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:04.140
How about you, Yousetsu Mask-san?

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:09.120
I'm 5,000 yen short.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:11.610
No way!

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.550
It has to be there!

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:14.280
Wait, let's count again.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.060
I'll help!

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:18.910
I keep getting a different amount from 
the machine when I count by hand.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.930
Oh crap, I hate huge discrepancies!

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:28.490
I'm so scared, I'm so 
scared, I'm so scared...

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.000
<i>Gasmask-senpai is terrified out of his mind.</i>

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.120
<b>Cash overage/shortage</b>

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.120
<b>Actual</b>

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.520
<i>Yes!</i>

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:36.290
<i>We're clear!</i>

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:37.660
We're at zero.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.860
Ah, thank goodness. That scared me.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.990
Bye, everyone.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:45.770
See you.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:50.970
<i>There's a ton of manga 
going out tomorrow, too.</i>

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.970
<b>Books to set up before opening</b>

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:53.590
Honda-san, ready to go?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:54.700
Yes.

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.220
That discrepancy scared me.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:01.780
No kidding.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.320
I seriously hate it when there's 
such a huge discrepancy.

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:10.510
<i>And that's how we end
 a day at the bookstore.</i>

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:14.850
<i>Here's hoping for another good day.</i>

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:15.790
<b>Returns</b>

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:15.790
<b>New books</b>

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:17.250
Good work today.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.500
See you tomorrow.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:27.210
<b>** Bookstore</b>

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.660
<i>I'll have to work hard tomorrow, too.</i>
